text With my bag still in my hand, I walk down the hallway.
text It feels really inappropriate to look like this this late.
text You can tell right away that I am either leaving early or have just arrived.
text Then again, since I'm walking toward the classrooms, I guess it's not hard to tell I got here late.
text If I go to the classroom, Ryou should be there.
text I honestly don't want to see her right now.
text I have no idea just how I'll react when I see her.
text I sigh as I look outside the window.
text The front yard enters my field of vision.
text Just yesterday, Ryou and I had lunch there.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...??
text I see two familiar silhouettes over at the stone fence.
text A girl with long hair and a girl with short hair are sitting next to each other, side by side.
text It's Kyou... and Ryou...
text Two faces that make my heart ache.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text What are they talking about...?
text Since they are right next to each other, I cannot imagine them not talking to each other at all.
text Suddenly, I recall everything that occurred yesterday.
text When I hugged Kyou in the rain yesterday...
text When Ryou hugged me, even though I was drenched...
text And how much it hurt when I finally knew how we all truly felt.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...Hm?
text Having stood there while looking down into the front yard for a while, I notice movement in my line of sight.
text They're... waving at me?
text @[Tomoya]
text ...
text Kyou is facing this way, and waving at me.
text Seeming to follow her sister's lead, Ryou is waving too.
text Then, Kyou beckons me over.
text @[Tomoya]
text ​~~~...
text I suppose there's no getting out of this one...
